 how did I come  around to it I think at that point I  just said yes absolutely and and I  walked out the door and then I went home  and I thought what have I done you know  you start immediately I started watching  footage of him all the archival footage  and I said well there's a reason they're  making a movie but there's also a reason  that only one person could do that and  it seemed like an impossible task  except I said listen you got one shot at  doing something living out your dream  someone offers you this and you have to  do it I thought about every other actor  who has as much talent and doesn't get  afforded these opportunities and you  just can't you can't let yourself down  you can't let anybody else down and I  thought hey it's a big risk but what's  life about and the spirit of Freddie you  take a little risk and see how it goes  Rami and Joe I can only imagine like the  YouTube wormholes you must have gone  down just to study you know how Freddie  carried himself on stage how John Deacon  moved with the bass guitar were you guys  looking for stuff that was just about  your individual person you know video  clips or were you finding stuff and  sending it to each other like oh yeah I  just found this you should watch this  yeah well I mean specifically live a it  I think there's like like 10 million  views of that on YouTube I think we're 5  million of them yeah it's fun well you  know it's sort of funny because it's  it's obviously when you go to youtube  and you watch that concert footage it's  like mostly Freddie right he's the  frontman he's the guy but that's what's  so great about actually being able to  make this movie in the age of the  Internet in the age of YouTube because  you can like go to concerts like famous  concerts they did and they have like the  John Deakin camera where you just follow  John Deakin for three hours and see what  he does for every single song some of  its not that interesting but you still  get to see all of it and s